# =================================================================
# CONFIGURATION FOR QWEN 3.6 35B A3B - APEX-MTP-I-Mini GGUF - CUDA MODE
# =================================================================
# Fastest profile measured on the GPU host: 97.2 tok/s (n=5) with --fit-target 384,
# 10/10 on the independent LRU-cache-with-TTL edge-case suite, 14.3GB on disk.
# That is +115% over the originally shipped Q4_K_XL / 2-slot / ctx-393216
# config's 45.1 tok/s, at equal code quality on the hardest task in this repo.
# (--fit-target 384 reaches 97.2 but leaves only ~599MiB of VRAM free, too thin
# for a GPU that also drives a Windows desktop -- see the compose file.)
# Three independent gains stack here: right-sized KV cache (1 slot x 128K),
# the APEX per-expert quant, and a --fit-target that actually uses the GPU.
#
# MODEL
# Same Qwen3.6-35B-A3B MoE weights as the champion profile (30 Gated DeltaNet +
# 10 full-attention layers, 256 experts routed 8-per-token, ~3B active), but
# quantized by mudler with APEX (Adaptive Precision for EXpert Models), which
# assigns precision per expert instead of uniformly. On this host the smaller
# footprint is what pays: at 14.3GB vs the champion's 22.9GB it leaves far more
# of the 23GB RAM ceiling free, and expert access stops being the bottleneck.
# The MTP head is bundled, verified active in the server log
# ("common_speculative_init_result: creating MTP draft context").
# Docker Compose file for GPU
COMPOSE_FILE=docker/docker-compose-gpu-qwen-35b-a3b-apex-mini-vision.yml

HF_REPO="mudler/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-APEX-MTP-GGUF"
HF_FILE="Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-APEX-MTP-I-Mini.gguf"

# --- Vision ---
# Same weights as the apex-mini profile; this file is what adds image and
# video input. It lives in the sibling APEX repo, not the MTP one, and is
# downloaded automatically by launch-server.sh (861 MB).
HF_MMPROJ_REPO="mudler/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-APEX-GGUF"
HF_MMPROJ_FILE="mmproj.gguf"

# Local host to access llama-server
LLAMA_HOST=127.0.0.1
# Local port to access llama-server
LLAMA_PORT=12345

# Context size (measured in tokens). 128K in a single slot.
LLAMA_CONTEXT_SIZE=131072

# CPU Threads (total threads - 2)
LLAMA_CPU_THREADS=14

# Local storage path for GGUF model files
MODELS_DIR=""

# -----------------------------------------------------------------
# CONCURRENCY TRADE-OFF
# -----------------------------------------------------------------
# This profile ships --parallel 1. Total KV-cache allocation -- not per-slot
# context -- turned out to be the dominant speed lever on this 23GB host, so
# adding slots costs real throughput even when each slot still gets its 128K:
#
#   APEX-I-Mini    --parallel 1 / ctx 131072  ->  79.1 tok/s
#   APEX-I-Compact --parallel 1 / ctx 131072  ->  75.7 tok/s
#   APEX-I-Compact --parallel 2 / ctx 262144  ->  64.3 tok/s   (2x 128K slots)
#   Q4_K_XL        --parallel 1 / ctx 131072  ->  60.8 tok/s
#   Q4_K_XL        --parallel 2 / ctx 393216  ->  45.1 tok/s   (shipped default)
#
# If you run concurrent subagents, switch to --parallel 2 with --ctx-size 262144
# in the compose file -- that keeps 128K per slot and still beats the current
# default by ~42%. Do NOT keep --ctx-size 393216 when raising --parallel: that
# allocates 3x the KV cache for no extra per-slot context.
